<title>BULGARIA: TENNIS-DAVIS CUP EURO/AFRICAN ZONE GROUP THREE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-DAVIS CUP EURO/AFRICAN ZONE GROUP THREE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PLOVDIV, Bulgaria 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the final</p>
<p>day in the Davis Cup Euro/African Zone group three tournament on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>Bulgaria beat Monaco 3-0</p>
<p>Results (Bulgarian names first):</p>
<p>Ivan Keskinov beat Christophe Bosio 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Orlin Stanoychev beat Sebastien Graeff 6-3 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>Ivo Bratanov/Ivailo Traikov beat Christophe  Boggeti/Sebastien</p>
<p>Graeff 6-7 (6-8) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Estonia beat Moldova 2-1</p>
<p>Results (Estonian names first)</p>
<p>Gert Vilms lost to Oleg Sinic 1-6 3-6</p>
<p>Rene Busch beat Juri Gorban 3-6 6-4 6-1</p>
<p>Andrei Luzgin/Gert Vilms beat Juri Gorban/Oleg Sinic 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Kenya beat Malta 2-1</p>
<p>Results (Kenyan names first)</p>
<p>Allan Cooper beat Gordon Asciak 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Paul Wekesa beat Mark Schembri 6-3 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>Allan Cooper/Norbert Odour lost to Gordon Asciak/Chris Gatt,</p>
<p>walkover</p>
<p>Algeria beat Cameroon 2-1</p>
<p>Results (Algerian names first)</p>
<p>Mohammed Mahmoudi lost to Angelin Mvogo 0-6 0-30 (Mahmoudi</p>
<p>retired injured)</p>
<p>Nourredine Mahmoudi beat Yann Auzoux 6-0 6-1</p>
<p>Noudjeim Hakimi/Nourredine Mahmoudi beat Yann Auzoux/Angelin</p>
<p>Mvogo 3-6 7-6 (9-7) 6-1</p>
<p>Final stanings:</p>
<p>1. Bulgaria</p>
<p>2. Monaco</p>
<p>3. Estonia</p>
<p>4. Moldova</p>
<p>5. Kenya</p>
<p>6. Malta</p>
<p>7. Algeria</p>
<p>8. Cameroon</p>
<p>Promoted to Euro/African zone group two: Bulgaria, Monaco</p>
<p>Relegated to Euro/African zone group four): Algeria,</p>
<p>Cameroon</p>
</text>
